course: dictionary
lesson: 14990
title: Represented: one thing standing for another
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Represent means to stand for something, or to act or speak for someone. «Each star represented 10 votes» means each star stood for 10 votes, so the star was a sign for a number. Represented is the past form, so it tells us this already happened.
explain: When someone represents a group, they speak or act for everyone in it. «Maya represented our school at the spelling contest» means she competed and spoke for the whole school, not just for herself. Ask yourself: who or what is standing in for whom?
explain: A picture, chart or model can also be represented. «The bars on the graph represented the number of rainy days.» Each bar shows a count, so the bar stands for the days. Use the words around the word to find out what the thing stands for.
fact: Represent means to stand for something, or to act or speak for someone.
fact: «Represented» is the past form of represent.
fact: «Each star represented 10 votes» means each star stood for 10 votes.
fact: «He represented his town in parliament» means he spoke and acted for the people of his town.
fact: «Is represented by» means shown or stood for by something else, as in «the town is represented by a red star on the map».
exercise: «Each star represented 10 votes.» What does represented mean here? | Was thrown away | *Stood for, as a sign of | Was counted twice | Was a bright, shiny shape
exercise: «Maya represented our school at the spelling contest.» Who did Maya speak and act for? | The judges | *Our school | Herself only | Her family's dog
exercise: «The bars on the graph represented the number of rainy days.» What do the bars stand for? | The colours of the rain | *The number of rainy days | The length of the lesson | The teachers
test: «The painting represented a stormy sea.» What was the painting showing? | A busy market | A sunny beach | *A stormy sea | A snowy mountain
test: Sam says represented means was missing. What does represented really mean? | Was hidden under a rug | *Stood for, or was shown as something | Was lost in the rain | Was left behind on the bus
exam: «He represented his town in parliament.» Which word is closest in meaning to represented here? | Hid from | Forgot | *Spoke and acted for | Ignored
